insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('p-two-writers-one-lane-refetch-main-s676b','pitfall','Two sessions worked slice B at once; re-fetch main before every dispatch','S676: Sam opened a session from a stale greeting (S672) at 14:21Z while the CPL Queue routine was working slice B under the same handoff (676). The interactive session read main once at start, then dispatched seven captures, restages, rereads and loads over three hours without re-fetching main, so it missed #3456 (merged 14:50Z). Its rereads replaced 43 unchecked rows (Cabrillo 30, Gavilan 3, Lemoore 5, San Mateo 5) with duplicate readings, and it spent a second, small extraction. Each reread receipt held main''s rows as before-values; migration s676b_reread_rollback (run 44136158970) restored all 43, confirmed by a live read. Rule: before each dispatch on a shared lane, git fetch origin main and read the newest handoff; a scheduled routine is a live writer that list_sessions does not show.',array['coordination','harvest','pitfall','slice-b'],'proposed','S676 second writer; #3456; receipt kb/receipts/migration_s676b_reread_rollback_44136158970.json',null,null,'S676 second writer','2026-11-17'),
('f-crafton-hills-11766-on-master-teacher-page-s676b','finding','Crafton Hills Teacher 11766 is filed on the Master Teacher page','S676: on main after #3456, Teacher 11766 (Certificate of Achievement, 16 to 30 units) is read from master-teacher-certificate-of-achievement, and fails. The catalog has its own page (credit-programs/child-development-cdev/teacher-certificate-of-achievement), which the self-test counts as a false match, so the lookup does not search at Crafton Hills. A fix places 11766 on its own page; until then, a fresh read extracts it again from the wrong page.',array['program-requirements','harvest','crafton-hills'],'proposed','S676 second writer; capture run 44103239951; main records/11766.json run 44090908924',null,null,'S676 second writer','2026-11-17')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

